                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 2]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">Article XI</hi></head>
                <p>Commercial travelers representing manufacturers, merchants and traders domiciled
                    in the territories of either High Contracting Party shall on their entry into
                    and sojourn in the territories of the other Party and on their departure
                    therefrom be accorded the most favored nation treatment in respect of customs
                    and other privileges and of all charges and taxes of whatever denomination
                    applicable to them or to their samples.</p>
                <p>If either High Contracting Party require the presentation of an authentic
                    document establishing the identity and authority of a commercial traveler, a
                    signed statement by the concern or concerns represented, certified by a consular
                    officer of the country of destination shall be accepted as satisfactory.</p>
            </div>
